# WHAT AN SDIST MUST NEVER CARRY.
#
# The `exclude` list under `[tool.setuptools.packages.find]` in pyproject.toml
# governs *package discovery*, which is the wheel's file set.  It does NOT
# govern an sdist: distutils' sdist command adds `tests/test*.py` and
# `test/test*.py` to every source distribution from a legacy default --
# `_add_defaults_optional()` in
# `.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/setuptools/_distutils/command/sdist.py`
# (the same rule exists in distutils itself).  Measured on this repo: without
# the rules below, `python -m build --sdist` ships 201 files under `tests/`,
# and adding `exclude = [...]` to pyproject.toml changes that number by zero.
#
# `prune` is processed after those defaults, so it is what actually removes
# them.  `tests` is the one that matters today; the rest are here so a
# development tree added later cannot start riding along by matching the same
# legacy glob (a top-level `test_*.py` under any of them would).
#
# NONE of this affects a checkout.  `prune` only filters the sdist's file list;
# `tests/` and `evals/` stay on disk, `pytest.ini`'s `testpaths = tests` is
# untouched, and both suites still run in place with `pytest tests/` and
# `pytest evals/`.
#
# Pinned by tests/test_prod_packaging_excludes_dev_trees.py.

prune tests
prune evals
prune scripts
prune examples
prune docs
prune deploy
prune templates
prune android
